  "goodToKnow": "Die Kaserne is a military barracks; English barracks is plural in form, but German Kaserne is a normal feminine singular. After the Cold War and the withdrawal of many Allied troops, numerous Kasernen were turned into housing, universities or business parks, a process called Konversion. Der Kasernenton is a harsh, barked tone of command. From French caserne. Plural: die Kasernen."
